  "template_id": "T-MOCK-SCREEN-first-session-landing-page-and-payers",
  "template_params": {
    "tables": "signups, sessions, subscriptions, payments",
    "cohort": "signups from 2025-07-01 to 2025-09-30",
    "fn": "ROW_NUMBER",
    "keep": 1
  },
  "sub_skill": null,
  "difficulty": "E3",
  "company": "mailvora",
  "schema": "mailvora",
  "edge_schema": "mailvora_edge_win",
  "prompt": "The growth team wants to know which landing pages start the journeys of new users, and how many of those users go on to pay. Take the users whose signup_ts, a moment in UTC, is from 1 July 2025 00:00 up to but not including 1 October 2025 00:00. A user's sessions are the sessions with the user's visitor_id, and the user's first session is the one with the earliest session_start, whenever it was. When two sessions of a user tie on session_start, the one with the lower session_id counts as the first. A user is a paying user when any of the user's subscriptions has a payment that was not refunded (refunded is false). For each landing_page, return four columns, in this order: landing_page; new_users, the number of those users whose first session started on that landing page; paying_users, how many of them are paying users; and paying_pct, 100 times paying_users divided by new_users, rounded to 1 decimal. Count each user once, and leave out users with no session. Sort by new_users from highest to lowest; when landing pages tie on new_users, by landing_page from A to Z.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "landing_page",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "new_users",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "paying_users",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "paying_pct",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
  "rules": {
    "order_matters": true,
    "sort_keys": [
      {
        "column": "new_users",
        "desc": true
      },
      {
        "column": "landing_page",
        "desc": false
      }
    ],
    "check_names": false,
    "allow_extra_columns": false,
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "landing_page",
        "type_class": "text",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      {
        "name": "new_users",
        "type_class": "numeric",
        "precision": "count"
      },
      {
        "name": "paying_users",
        "type_class": "numeric",
        "precision": "count"
      },
      {
        "name": "paying_pct",
        "type_class": "numeric",
        "precision": "ratio",
        "require_rounding": 1
      }
    ],
    "strict_temporal_type": false,
    "trim_strings": false,
    "tie_policy": "none",
    "key_columns": [
      "landing_page"
    ],
    "timeout_ms": 5000,
    "set_semantics": false,
    "case_insensitive": false,
    "strict_column_order": false
  },
  "hints": [
    "Next, number each new user's sessions from the earliest, keep the first one, and count the users by its landing page.",
    "A filter on a numbered row belongs in an outer query, not in the WHERE of the query that numbers it; and a user with many payments must still count once."
  ],
